Z||000011||PAUL88GT||06-13-2000||10:30 AM||||My 88GT probably has more red on it that any other one. I have only had the car less than a year. It is bright red metallic. Ed Parks of the Fiero Factory could provide the specific name of the paint. I am very happy with it. The new paint is three or four years old and holding up very well. Hope this post works since it is my first one. <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/004_4.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/002_2.jpg"> <P>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 06-13-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by PAUL88GT (edited 06-13-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000012||Raydar||06-13-2000||11:54 AM||||Paul, <BR>Nice job! <P>Was your car painted by one of Ed's associates? <BR>I believe he uses a Maaco, local to his shop. They do some really nice work.<P>Is yours a basecoat/clearcoat job, or one step? <BR>How close is it to the stock "bright red"?<BR>Looks *very* close in the pic. <P>Thanks!  Steve<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 06-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||TheFiero64||06-13-2000||12:26 PM||||Red, Red, Red...... I love Red.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000014||PAUL88GT||06-13-2000||01:18 PM||||Raydar:<BR>I believe it was the local Maaco shop, but Ed watched over the process closely.<P>I am not sure about the process. I know it was very expensive paint. You would have to contact Ed directly.  It is a very fine metallic and can only be seen very close in the sunlight. <P>Although not clear in the scanned photo, it is slightly brighter that the factory red.  Also, it was an overcast day when I snapped the photos.<P>I plan to bring it to the FOCOA nationals in Louisville as a spectator in July.<BR>Paul||||reg||1
